I've seen quite a few monsters quaffing potions of healing, gain level (bummer)
as well as others including good scrolls, zapping good wands.

However I'm yet to see a monster do anything bad, like quaff paralasis, or
zap me with speed monster or read destroy armor.  I even tossed some non
cursed destroy armor's at some dwarves; they didn't touch em.  Throw em a
teleport and they're off.  It seems a bit one-sided to me, as the average
dwarve who has been hapily  spending his life playing with pickaxes in the
gnome mines shouldn't be that well educated.  (Then again what would happen if
the monster you were attacking read a scroll of taming?)

Some of the more stupid monsters should attack each other more often as well,
i mean your basic feline (jaguar type size) shouldn't be so discerning about
who it attacks in a multi-monster melee, in fact it would be more likey to
go for smaller prey, as well as going for the prey that is hitting back the
least (after moving away from the worst attackers.)  Even your own pet gets
less attention from attackers, why should an agressive housecat be more
interested in me that my own moggie on its territory?

By the way, if you undefine POLYSELF the compilation fails, and the only
thing that pisses me off in this game is rolling along in nice new shiny
armor and loosing the lot because of a !$^@* polymorph trap (usually at
least one per Gnomish Mine.)  It's the only reason I started cheating, I find
that sort of trap shouldn't appear so early on.

Finally the fact that there is never a *#&@ tengu around when you need one
(perhaps an internal list of what a player needs could be kept, and associate
it with luck as to how likely it is to appear would be nice and save much
hanging around.)

But overall, its very good, the good points far outweigh the bad points.

